You push through the wall of tall, odorous plants. A strong, sickly sweet smell surrounds you from all sides, shrouding you in its scent. It feels as though you're parting not just the stems, but the very wall of smell, which is almost tangible. It's very damp here, and the ground is slippery. But the objective appears to be so close, and you're stubbornly marching forward.

Despite the inconveniences, you advance pretty fast. It's strange, but you have no more worries about your fate; even the scary night in the forest comes to your mind as if it had happened long ago to somebody else. Somehow you start thinking that as soon as you reach water, your adventure will be over, you will find Snoopy, and go home to take a nap.

Yeah, it's a good idea - to take a nap... A slight wind is blowing; waves are running through the meadow, and the ground doesn't seem damp anymore. Maybe you should really take a nap. Just half an hour...